  "body": "**Stacked on #1131** (#541 sinker burn to depth, branch `issue/541-sinker-burn-depth`), which is itself stacked on #560 (#531 EDM condition table), stacked on #551 (#530 EDM machine kinds). The chain is #551 -> #560 -> #1131 -> this PR. Until those merge, their commits show here; this PR adds one commit on top of #1131's head. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- **A wear rate per condition.** `edm.conditions[]` gains an optional `wear`: the electrode's axial wear rate, as mm of electrode lost per mm burned (dimensionless, not unit-scaled). `parse_mch` (so `LoadMachine` and the project reader) and `Edm::is_sane` refuse a rate that is not a finite ratio in [0, 1), by name (\"... is not an axial wear rate ...\"). No rate ships with any machine; rates are user data (#290 D4).\n- **A measured wear and a layer step on the op.** `SinkerBurnOp` gains `layer`, `wear_lost` and `wear_over`. A wear measured between burns (length lost over depth burned) wins over the condition's rate. With neither stated, the burn is **not compensated**: the path note and the op page say `electrode wear: not compensated (no wear rate stated)`. `CreateOperation` / `EditOperationParams` (and the project reader) refuse a measured rate of 1 or more, a half-stated or non-finite measurement, and a non-positive layer step, all by name, through a new `OpParams::named_refusal` door that runs ahead of the generic \"not usable\".\n- **Compensation in Z** (`crates/motion/src/sinker_wear.rs`, `burn_compensated`). The burn is fed in layers. Each layer's tip is programmed `rate * d` deeper, where `d` is how far that layer's nominal floor lies below the work top. Every move is re-checked against the bound: the stated floor plus the gap, minus `rate` times the stated depth. A move past it is refused as over-deep, by name. All of #541's refusals still apply. The electrode-length law now reads the deeper, compensated tip. With no rate and no layer step, the moves are exactly #541's (pinned).\n- **The stock sim judges the worn electrode.** `plan_program` maps each programmed tip back to where the worn electrode burns (`worn_tip`, the exact inverse of the compensation). A compensated burn to the cavity's own floor therefore reads 0 gouge cells, and a nominal floor past the model is still convicted.\n- **Staleness.** The op digest adds the layer step and the measured wear, and the stamp adds the condition's rate, each only when stated. Existing digests do not change.\n- **File, MCP, UI.** The three op keys are additive and optional: older files load unchanged and write no new keys. MCP drives them through the existing params JSON door (`add_operation` / `edit_operation`). No new command or tool was needed, and a test pins this. The Sinker Burn page's Passes tab gains Layer step, Measured wear and Measured over, plus the compensation status line.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/546-sinker-wear-comp.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/sinker_wear.rs`:\n  - `sinker_wear_layers_match_golden`: golden `crates/app/tests/golden/sinker_wear_layers.cl`. I read it: three 2 mm layers at rate 0.02, gap 0.05, with tips at Z 18.010, 15.970 and 13.930 (that is 18.05 - 0.04, 16.05 - 0.08 and 14.05 - 0.12).\n  - `a_condition_wear_rate_deepens_each_layer_and_the_sim_judges_it_clean`\n  - `a_missing_wear_rate_shows_not_compensated`\n  - `a_bad_wear_rate_is_refused_by_name`: machine file and op commands.\n  - `a_measured_wear_wins_over_the_condition_and_round_trips_the_file`: includes an older file with no new keys.\n  - `the_wear_fields_ride_the_mcp_params_door`\n- Unit tests in `motion::sinker_wear`: wear off equals the plain burn, per-layer deepening plus its inverse, and refusals of the rate, step and reach.\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_burn.rs`: the op literal gains the three new `None` fields; no assertion changed.\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on this head (b0e121ce), 24.3 min. The tools, post, sim, motion and ui suites pass. In the app suites, every binary passes except one test, and that test **fails on #1131's own head too**: I ran it alone on `origin/issue/541-sinker-burn-depth`, and this PR doesn't change it:\n  - `coarse_laws::every_kind_is_either_judged_or_refused_for_a_stated_reason_on_a_reduced_model`: \"SinkerBurn is judged while a tolerance is left\". The fidelity law refuses a Sinker Burn on a reduced-fidelity model, but the test expects it to be judged.\n  The fix belongs on #1131. The sinker_burn, sinker_wear, edm_machine, edm_conditions, golden_cl and project_roundtrip suites pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control** (#290 D10). The conditions and wear rates are synthetic fixtures.\n- Wear is axial only; corner and side wear are not modelled. No orbit (#544), no multi-electrode undersize logic (#543), and no sinker post (#542). Layers are a stepped plunge with no retract between them.\n- The field-arm stock view still refuses an electrode program (as in #541).\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM: electrode wear compensation in Z - a stated axial wear rate (per condition in the machine file, or measured on the op) deepens each burn layer by the wear it states, bounded and refused by name past it; with no rate the burn says \"not compensated\" (#546)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #546\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
